  "notes": "Source: Auguste Escoffier School of Culinary Arts-Boulder Catalog 2025-2026, Volume 33 (published 10/2/2025), official program tables (verified via escoffier.edu 2026-10-01). Residential and distance-learning AOS Baking and Pastry tables are course-for-course identical (same courses, modules, credits, 90 quarter-credit total), so one plan covers both delivery modes. Program tables carry genuine quarter + 6-week module columns (module = term); four courses span two modules and are placed in their first module: PA102 (modules 1-2), PA120 (3-4), PA130 (5-6), PA220 (7-8). The residential table prints 'Confiserie and Artisian Baking'; the distance table and the PA130 course-description heading print 'Confiserie and Artisan Baking' (used here). Asterisks on CE187/CE167/CE129/CE161 in the residential table are catalog footnote markers ('*CE135 Restaurant Operations equates to: CE187, CE167, and CE129' and '**CE161 Building Your Own Business equates to: CE160'); codes recorded without footnote marks. PA296 hours differ slightly between tables (residential: 0/180/180; distance: 9/0/171/180) with identical 180 total hours and 6 credits. Externship courses require completion of all other program courses with a 2.0 or higher GPA unless permission is granted by the Vice President of Academic Affairs (OP290: 'unless permission is granted by the Program Lead'), per the catalog's course-description section.",
